file=People & Culture/grove/operational/commands/grove-commands.md · h=<!--\nOperational: commands file for grove (People & Culture / Learning & Development)\nper §7 commands/.\n\n§7 rule: document structure/layout is universal across every agent's commands file\n(same table shape, same sections). Actual triggers, shortcuts, and precedence rules\ninside are unique to grove's 4-skill roster.\n\nTrigger content pulled verbatim from each skill's `## When to Use` section — this file\nconsolidates, not invents.\n-->\n · g—c:grove — Commands=Natural-language triggers, slash shortcuts, and precedence for grove (People & Culture /\nLearning & Development). Triggers come from each skill's `## When to Use` section — this\nfile consolidates, not invents.\n · ss:Slash Shortcuts=Convenience layer for common single-skill invocations. Slash shortcuts are optional; every\nskill also fires on the natural-language triggers below.\n · tb=\| Shortcut \| Fires \| One-line purpose \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `/grove-gap [team]` \| `skill-gap-map` full 5-step \| End-to-end skills gap analysis for a team \| · tb=\| `/grove-gap-quick [role]` \| `skill-gap-map` Phases 1–4 only \| Fast matrix + gap calculation; skip action recommendation for now \| · tb=\| `/grove-matrix [team]` \| `skill-gap-map` § Skills Matrix & Scoring \| Build the 1–5 proficiency matrix for a team \| · tb=\| `/grove-priority [gap list]` \| `skill-gap-map` Phases 5–6 + `skill_gap.py` \| Compute priority_score (gap × criticality) + rank top-3 to top-5 \| · tb=\| `/grove-action [gap]` \| `skill-gap-map` Phase 7 + `skill_gap.py` `recommend_action()` \| Build / Buy / Borrow / Bridge recommendation per top-priority gap \| · tb=\| `/grove-program [gap or Level-4 result]` \| `training-program-design` full sequence \| End-to-end program design (ADDIE + 70-20-10 + Kirkpatrick evaluation plan) \| · tb=\| `/grove-addie [scope]` \| `training-program-design` § ADDIE Phases \| Design across ADDIE's 5 phases explicitly \| · tb=\| `/grove-kirkpatrick [program]` \| `training-program-design` § Kirkpatrick Levels + `training_program.py` \| Backward-design evaluation plan Levels 4→1 \| · tb=\| `/grove-70-20-10 [program]` \| `training-program-design` § 70-20-10 + `training_program.py` `allocation_check()` \| Check allocation against target; flag imbalances \| · tb=\| `/grove-timing [months + level]` \| `training-program-design` + `training_program.py` `kirkpatrick_timing_ok()` \| Is it the right time to reliably measure Kirkpatrick Level X? \| · tb=\| `/grove-drivers [program]` \| `training-program-design` Phase 4 required-drivers check \| Confirm management support / systems / accountability structure before build \| · tb=\| `/grove-dp [skill]` \| `deliberate-practice` § Instructions Phases 1–4 \| Component decomposition + feedback loop + difficulty + repetition for a target skill \| · tb=\| `/grove-dp-framework [context]` \| `deliberate-practice` § Purpose brief \| Short DP-lens framing when only theory-level input is needed \| · tb=\| `/grove-enrollment [training + cohort]` \| `training-operations` Instructions Step 2 \| Define enrollment automation rules for a training program \| · tb=\| `/grove-audit-trail [record or program]` \| `training-operations` Step 3 + `training_ops.py` `validate_audit_trail()` \| Validate compliance records against 4 required fields \| · tb=\| `/grove-expiry [certification list]` \| `training-operations` Step 5 + `training_ops.py` `expiry_alert_status()` \| Compute renewal-alert bands (EXPIRED / URGENT / ALERT / OK) \| · tb=\| `/grove-compliance-report [scope]` \| `training-operations` Step 6 + `training_ops.py` `rollup_completion_counts()` \| Roll up completion / compliance status by department / venture \| · tb=\| `/grove-access-audit [system]` \| `training-operations` Step 7 + Principle 8 \| Audit the audit-trail system's current access-control roster; route change recommendations to veil + operator \| · mcs:Multi-Skill Chain Shortcuts=Common flows touching more than one skill.\n · tb=\| Chain shortcut \| Sequence \| Purpose \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `/grove-gap-to-build [scope]` \| `skill-gap-map` full (Phases 1–7) → if Phase-7 action = Build → `deliberate-practice` component decomposition + feedback loop → `training-program-design` full sequence with DP output as input to Phase 3 \| End-to-end Build action from gap identification through program design \| · tb=\| `/grove-compliance-rollout [training + cohort]` \| `training-operations` Steps 1–8 for a new mandatory training in a new scope: single-system confirm → enrollment automation → 4-field audit-trail capture → retention-period confirm (route to counsel) → expiry alert setup → completion rollup dashboard → access-control setup with veil → escalate-patterns rule active \| End-to-end rollout of a new mandatory training with full compliance discipline \| · tb=\| `/grove-audit-response [scope + time-window]` \| `training-operations` Step 3 (validate all records in window) → Step 6 (rollup by group) → Step 4 confirm (retention still valid for the specific regulation) → produce audit-response artifact \| Compliance-audit response preparation from the audit-trail system \| · tb=\| `/grove-new-role-onboarding [role]` \| `skill-gap-map` for the role's required capabilities → Build action recommendation → `training-program-design` for onboarding program → `training-operations` enrollment automation triggered by hire-date \| Onboarding-scoped chain from hiring-kit's post-accept handoff \| · tb=\| `/grove-competence-intervention [team]` \| Handoff from `motivation-map` Phase-5 competence-need diagnosis → `skill-gap-map` to identify the specific skill → Build action → `deliberate-practice` for practice loop → `training-program-design` for program shell \| Competence-need routing from maslow's motivation-map \| · mcs:Multi-Skill Chain Shortcuts=**Chain shortcuts respect §0.2.** Each phase produces its own artifact and gets its own\nreview moment when the operator requests one. Chains are convenience routes for the\nsequence, not approval to batch outputs.\n · nt(:Natural-Language Triggers (by skill)=Pulled from each skill's `## When to Use`.\n · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "deliberate practice" / "Ericsson framework" / "component-skill decomposition" \| Direct hit — mechanism-level framework \| · tb=\| "how do people actually learn this" / "why isn't the training working" \| Direct hit — mechanism diagnostic \| · tb=\| "design a real practice loop" / "design a feedback loop for [skill]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "comfort zone plus one" / "the practice isn't stretching them" \| Direct hit — difficulty calibration \| · tb=\| "10,000 hours" \| Push back per Principle 3 — no specific hour count quoted as authority \| · tb=\| Handoff from `training-program-design` Phase 3 (mechanism-level design for 70% and 20%) \| System-triggered \| · tb=\| Handoff from `motivation-map` Phase 5 (competence-need intervention) \| System-triggered — via `skill-gap-map` typically \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "skills matrix for [team / role / venture]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "skills gap analysis" / "capability assessment for [team]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "what skills does this team need" / "how big is the [X] skill gap" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "hire vs upskill" / "build buy borrow bridge" \| Direct hit — the 4-way routing \| · tb=\| "prioritize which skill gap to address first" \| Direct hit — Phase 5-6 \| · tb=\| "business case for this new role / this training investment" \| Direct hit — feeds decision with gap data \| · tb=\| "catalog every skill in the org" \| Push back per Fallback rule 3 (unscoped inventory) \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "design a training program to close [gap]" \| Direct hit — Build action from skill-gap-map \| · tb=\| "training program for [role / competency]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "build a development plan / stretch assignment structure for [succession candidate]" \| Direct hit — from future merit \| · tb=\| "design an evaluation plan for [program]" \| Direct hit — Kirkpatrick backward design \| · tb=\| "did [program] actually work" / "evaluate training effectiveness" \| Direct hit — Kirkpatrick 4-levels evaluation \| · tb=\| "ADDIE" / "70-20-10 design" / "Kirkpatrick evaluation" \| Direct hit — framework-specific \| · tb=\| "just build me a course" \| Push back per Fallback rule 5 (10%-only pattern violates 70-20-10) \| · tb=\| "measure behavior change 2 weeks after training" \| Push back per Fallback rule 2 (too-early, unreliable) \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "enrollment automation" for a training program \| Direct hit — Step 2 \| · tb=\| "compliance audit trail" (build, audit, investigate) \| Direct hit — Steps 3+8 \| · tb=\| "certification expiry" / "renewal alerts" \| Direct hit — Step 5 \| · tb=\| "training compliance report" for a department / venture \| Direct hit — Step 6 \| · tb=\| "audit training records" ahead of a regulatory request \| Direct hit — Step 3 validation \| · tb=\| "LMS setup for [scope]" \| Direct hit — Step 1 (system-of-record) \| · tb=\| "edit this audit-trail entry" / "delete this record" \| **HARD REFUSAL** per Principle 6 — corrections appended as new entries only \| · tb=\| "broaden read access to the audit-trail system" \| Escalate per Fallback rule 6 — veil + operator countersign required \| · tb=\| Handoff from `hiring-kit` (new-hire enrollment trigger) \| System-triggered \| · tb=\| Handoff from `payroll-and-eor` (worker classification determines training rules) \| System-triggered \| · pr(:Precedence Rules (when triggers overlap)=Full precedence in `operational/skill/grove-skill-routing.md § Trigger Precedence`. Load-bearing\ncalls restated:\n · tb=\| Overlap \| Winner \| Reason \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Ambiguous "training" without other context \| Push back — clarify content-design (training-program-design) vs logistics (training-operations) \| Different data models: aggregate vs individually-identifiable \| · tb=\| Ambiguous "L&D" \| `skill-gap-map` first (validate the gap exists), THEN routes to build/buy/borrow/bridge \| skill-gap-map is grove's analytical entry point \| · tb=\| Ambiguous "practice" \| `deliberate-practice` for mechanism-level; `training-program-design` for program shell that consumes it \| Bidirectional \| · tb=\| "audit training records" / "check if X completed [training]" \| `training-operations` always \| Compliance-scope is exclusive to training-operations \| · tb=\| Any request colliding with **individual crisis signal** in context \| **HARD ESCALATION — no skill fires** \| Universal Principle 3 (inherited); load-bearing safety rule \| · tb=\| Any request to **edit / delete existing audit-trail entry** \| **HARD REFUSAL** — Universal Principle 4 \| Cross-cutting audit-trail immutability rule; no operator override \| · tb=\| Any request to broaden audit-trail access without countersign \| Escalate to veil + operator \| Universal Principle 5 — access-control direction always tightening \| · tb=\| Compensation / workload-driven signal masquerading as training request \| Push back per Universal Principle 7 — route structural-first \| training-program-design Fallback rule 4; skill-gap-map Fallback rule 5 \| · n(t:Not-a-Command (routes to another agent)=Phrases that sound like they might trigger grove but route elsewhere per\n`grove-skill-routing.md § Cross-Agent Escalation Routing`.\n · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Route to \| Rationale \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| **ANY signal of individual crisis / self-harm / serious distress** (rare in grove context but possible via compliance conversation) \| **HARD BOUNDARY: Manager + HR Ops + EAP** \| Universal Principle 3 — immediate escalation, no exceptions, no operator override \| · tb=\| **"Edit this audit-trail entry" / "delete this record"** (rephrased) \| **HARD REFUSAL** — corrections appended as new entries only \| Universal Principle 4 — cross-cutting hard rule \| · tb=\| "assess this individual's mental health" / "how is [person] doing" \| **Operator + external professional** \| Aggregate-only rule (except the training-operations compliance-audit-trail scope, which is not for mental-health assessment) \| · tb=\| "review [person]'s performance" / "coach [person] through [issue]" \| **Future `merit` agent** (P&C sibling); currently → operator \| Individual perf out of grove's scope \| · tb=\| "team morale check" / "burnout signals" / "recognition program" \| **`maslow`** (P&C sibling) \| Motivation/wellbeing/recognition — maslow's scope \| · tb=\| "hire externally for [role]" / "open a req" (Buy action) \| **`hiring-kit`** (custom, hire) \| Downstream from skill-gap-map's Buy action \| · tb=\| "contractor for [role]" (Borrow action) \| **`payroll-and-eor`** (custom, hire) \| Downstream — W-2/1099/EOR classification \| · tb=\| "redeploy [person] to [role]" (Bridge action) \| **`workforce-planning`** (custom, hire) \| Downstream — structural / headcount move \| · tb=\| "which ATS should we use" / "ATS platform selection" \| **`ats-selection`** (custom, hire) \| Not grove's scope \| · tb=\| "compensation for [role]" / "pay-equity audit" / "comp benchmarking" \| **`payroll-and-eor`** (custom, hire) OR future `comp-benchmarking` \| Recognition/training never fix a comp problem \| · tb=\| "approve this training budget" \| **`board`** (Governance — fiduciary-guard skill) \| Spend-approval gate; grove produces cost, board approves \| · tb=\| "cross-jurisdiction retention rules for [training]" \| **Future Global Expansion department** (task #3); currently → operator + employment counsel \| Multi-jurisdiction footprint expands there \| · tb=\| "aggregate psychosocial-risk trends from compliance training" \| **Future Risk & ESG department** (task #6); currently → hold and log \| ISO 45003 governance route \| · tb=\| "time-to-fill" / "cost-per-hire" / "voluntary turnover" / "engagement metrics" \| **Future `Shared OS: people-analytics-metrics`** (task #12) \| Shared skill — grove references it but doesn't own \| · tb=\| "PII / GDPR question in the LMS or audit-trail system" \| **`veil`** (Cybersecurity — data protection) \| Data-protection scope \| · tb=\| "SSO / SCIM setup for the LMS" \| **`keyring`** (Cybersecurity — IAM) \| IAM scope \| · tb=\| "configure the LMS" / "grant permissions" / "vendor integration change" \| **Operator** \| grove produces the design and audit, not the click-through config \| · tb=\| "harassment signal in a training completion comment" \| **Operator + employment counsel** \| Legal fence — BUT if the same content contains individual crisis, HARD BOUNDARY escalation fires first \| · tb=\| Sibling P&C requests clearly belonging to hire \| **`hire`** (P&C Lead) \| Return with route \| · in:Interaction Notes=- **Slash shortcuts are optional.** grove fires on natural-language triggers too.\n- **Chain shortcuts respect §0.2.** Each phase artifact gets its own review moment.\n- **Every command runs through Universal Principle 11** (verification-before-completion)\nbefore its output ships.\n- **Every command routes through Universal Principle 3 first.** If an individual crisis\nsignal is present anywhere in the context, no grove skill fires — the escalation lane\ntakes over immediately.\n- **Audit-trail edit/delete requests are HARD REFUSED.** Not a discretionary block — the\nrefusal is baked into the tool_permissions in `grove-config.md § 9` and enforced across\nevery grove skill.\n- **Broadening audit-trail access requires countersign.** Not a discretionary block — the\nrouting is baked into `grove-config.md § 1 access_control` and requires veil + operator\ndocumented rationale.\n- **Charter-conflict routes to operator + veil.** Any command that would produce a\nCharter-conflicting output (e.g., an LMS integration that would put SSNs in a way that\nviolates data-protection rail) blocks and escalates.\n- **`grove-config.md § 1` audit-trail governance `<FILL_IN>`s block specific rollout\nwork.** Unfilled access-control roster or unpopulated retention-periods blocks the\naffected rollout, not just announces loud per §14.7.\n · m:Meta=- Compiled per §14.2 into the tier-2+ preamble of each of grove's 4 skills as the trigger table.\n- Structure (same section shape as every other agent's commands file) matches the §7\nuniversal layout; triggers/shortcuts/precedence are grove-specific.\n- Peer P&C agents (maslow already shipped with own commands file; merit pending) will\nhave their own commands files with the same layout and their own triggers/shortcuts.\n